dashboard.definition:
{
  "title": "AI Session Time Accounting",
  "description": "Where every second of a session went: TOOL_EXEC, SUBAGENT_WAIT, MODEL_ACTIVE_CONFIRMED, MODEL_ACTIVE_UNVERIFIED, HUMAN_IDLE, SYSTEM_OVERHEAD. Leave Session ID as * for a fleet-wide rollup.",
  "defaults": {
    "dataSources": {
      "ds.search": {
        "options": {
          "queryParameters": {
            "earliest": "$global_time.earliest$",
            "latest": "$global_time.latest$"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "inputs": {
    "input_timerange": {
      "type": "input.timerange",
      "options": {
        "token": "global_time",
        "defaultValue": "-7d@d,now"
      },
      "title": "Time Range"
    },
    "input_session": {
      "type": "input.text",
      "title": "Session ID (* = fleet-wide)",
      "options": {
        "token": "session_tok",
        "defaultValue": "*"
      }
    }
  },
  "dataSources": {
    "ds_base_category_totals": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "options": {
        "query": "`claude_time_accounting_by_gap($session_tok|s$)` | eventstats sum(gap_sec) as total_gap | eval pct=round(gap_sec/total_gap*100,1)"
      },
      "name": "Base: Category Totals"
    },
    "ds_category_table": {
      "type": "ds.chain",
      "options": {
        "extend": "ds_base_category_totals",
        "query": "| rename time_category as Category, gap_min as Minutes, turns as Turns, pct as \"% of Total\" | fields Category, Minutes, Turns, \"% of Total\" | sort - Minutes"
      },
      "name": "Category Totals"
    },
    "ds_category_bar": {
      "type": "ds.chain",
      "options": {
        "extend": "ds_base_category_totals",
        "query": "| rename time_category as Category, gap_min as Minutes | fields Category, Minutes | sort - Minutes"
      },
      "name": "Category Time (min)"
    },
    "ds_base_top_gaps": {
      "type": "ds.search",
      "options": {
        "query": "`claude_index` sourcetype=claude:code* type=assistant sessionId=$session_tok|s$ | sort 0 source -_time | streamstats current=f last(_time) as nxt by source | eval gap=nxt-_time | where isnotnull(gap) | spath path=\"message.content{}.name\" output=tool | spath path=\"message.content{}.type\" output=ctype | spath path=\"message.content{}.text\" output=text_mv | spath path=\"message.content{}.thinking\" output=thinking_mv | eval output_chars=coalesce(len(mvjoin(text_mv,\"\")),0)+coalesce(len(mvjoin(thinking_mv,\"\")),0) | eval time_category=case(isnotnull(mvfind(tool,\"Agent\")) OR isnotnull(mvfind(tool,\"Task\")),\"SUBAGENT_WAIT\", isnotnull(tool),\"TOOL_EXEC\", isnotnull(mvfind(ctype,\"text\")),\"HUMAN_IDLE\", gap<2,\"SYSTEM_OVERHEAD\", output_chars>0,\"MODEL_ACTIVE_CONFIRMED\", 1=1,\"MODEL_ACTIVE_UNVERIFIED\") | eval label=coalesce(mvjoin(tool,\",\"), time_category) | stats max(gap) as gap_sec values(time_category) as Category values(label) as Label values(sessionId) as \"Session ID\" by _time, source | eval \"Gap (min)\"=round(gap_sec/60,1), Started=strftime(_time,\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\") | sort - gap_sec | head 25 | rename source as Source | fields Started, \"Session ID\", Source, Category, Label, \"Gap (min)\""
      },
      "name": "Base: Top Individual Gaps"
    }
  },
  "visualizations": {
    "viz_category_bar": {
      "type": "splunk.bar",
      "title": "Time by Category (minutes)",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_category_bar"
      },
      "options": {}
    },
    "viz_category_table": {
      "type": "splunk.table",
      "title": "Category Totals",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_category_table"
      },
      "options": {}
    },
    "viz_top_gaps": {
      "type": "splunk.table",
      "title": "Longest Individual Gaps",
      "dataSources": {
        "primary": "ds_base_top_gaps"
      },
      "options": {},
      "eventHandlers": [
        {
          "type": "drilldown.setToken",
          "options": {
            "tokens": [
              {
                "token": "session_tok",
                "value": "row.Session ID.value"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "viz_documentation": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "**Two modes** — set **Session ID** to drill into one session (sum of gaps across its main file and any subagent files sharing that `sessionId`); leave it at `*` for a fleet-wide rollup of the same 6 categories across every session in `index=claude` over the selected time range.\n\n**Categories** — `TOOL_EXEC` (Bash/Read/MCP tool calls), `SUBAGENT_WAIT` (spawned subagent), `MODEL_ACTIVE_CONFIRMED` (no tool/no text, but this row's own text/thinking content is non-empty — real evidence of generation), `MODEL_ACTIVE_UNVERIFIED` (same, but this row's content is empty), `HUMAN_IDLE` (handed back, awaiting input), `SYSTEM_OVERHEAD` (unclassified gaps under 2s). The 2s `SYSTEM_OVERHEAD` cutoff is a starting guess from the shared `claude_time_accounting_by_gap` TA macro — tune it if this dashboard's data shows a different natural threshold.\n\n**Why the split** — verified directly against production: 100% of rows that reach the old single `MODEL_ACTIVE` branch had empty thinking content — Claude Code logs an empty placeholder `thinking` block as its own row, with real content landing on a separate row moments later. A single confident `MODEL_ACTIVE` number therefore overstated what this gap shape can prove; `MODEL_ACTIVE_CONFIRMED` will read near-zero here by construction, which is accurate, not a bug.\n\n**Known limitation** — classification is per-`source` (one session/subagent JSONL file) in isolation. A `HUMAN_IDLE`-looking gap in the main session that actually overlapped with a concurrently-running subagent in a *different* `source` file is not reclassified as `SUBAGENT_WAIT` — that needs cross-file timestamp-window correlation this gap/streamstats pattern can't do.\n\nClick a row in **Longest Individual Gaps** to drill that session into every panel."
      }
    }
  },
  "layout": {
    "type": "grid",
    "options": {},
    "structure": [
      {"item": "viz_category_bar", "type": "block", "position": {"x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 600, "h": 300}},
      {"item": "viz_category_table", "type": "block", "position": {"x": 600, "y": 0, "w": 600, "h": 300}},
      {"item": "viz_top_gaps", "type": "block", "position": {"x": 0, "y": 300, "w": 1200, "h": 360}},
      {"item": "viz_documentation", "type": "block", "position": {"x": 0, "y": 660, "w": 1200, "h": 220}}
    ],
    "globalInputs": ["input_timerange", "input_session"]
  }
}
